--TEST--
A `foreach` key binding over an `array<T>` is declared `string` or refused where it is written — `rule:types/arrays`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/arrays`: "every key is a `string`. There is no integer key." So an
// array's key binding is not an unprovable narrowing — it is the one type the
// container stores, and every other declared type is always wrong. Before
// `E0723` each of these type-checked and then tripped `nvs-ir`'s own
// assertion, which named a compiler gap for a mistake in the program.
array<int> $a = ["x" => 1, "y" => 2];

// The accepted spelling, written first: a position that stops being accepted
// fails here rather than as a missing refusal below.
foreach ($a as string $ok => int $v1) {
    echo $ok, "=", $v1, "\n";
}

// `int` is PHP's own key type and the mistake a port makes.
foreach ($a as int $ki => int $v2) {
    echo $v2, "\n";
}

foreach ($a as uint $ku => int $v3) {
    echo $v3, "\n";
}

// `mixed` is `rule:types/conversion`'s one unchecked position and still wrong here:
// there is no second key type for it to be the union of.
foreach ($a as mixed $km => int $v4) {
    echo $v4, "\n";
}

foreach ($a as int|string $kn => int $v5) {
    echo $v5, "\n";
}

// A nested array's inner key is the same question one level in.
array<array<int>> $grid = ["r" => ["c" => 1]];
foreach ($grid as string $r => array<int> $row) {
    foreach ($row as int $c => int $v6) {
        echo $c, $v6, "\n";
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";

// This marker sits last on purpose: every line above it is named by a line
// number in the expected diagnostic below.
// covers: lang:statements/foreach
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0723]: an array's key binding is a `string`, not `int`
   --> %s:16:16
   |
16 | foreach ($a as int $ki => int $v2) {
   |                ^^^^^^^ this binds as `int`
   = help: `rule:types/arrays` gives an `array<T>` one stored key type — every key is a `string`, and `$a[8]` is normalised to `$a["8"]` at the subscript rather than converted — so write `string $k`, and convert inside the body if the loop wants another type

error[E0723]: an array's key binding is a `string`, not `uint`
   --> %s:20:16
   |
20 | foreach ($a as uint $ku => int $v3) {
   |                ^^^^^^^^ this binds as `uint`
   = help: `rule:types/arrays` gives an `array<T>` one stored key type — every key is a `string`, and `$a[8]` is normalised to `$a["8"]` at the subscript rather than converted — so write `string $k`, and convert inside the body if the loop wants another type

error[E0723]: an array's key binding is a `string`, not `mixed`
   --> %s:26:16
   |
26 | foreach ($a as mixed $km => int $v4) {
   |                ^^^^^^^^^ this binds as `mixed`
   = help: `rule:types/arrays` gives an `array<T>` one stored key type — every key is a `string`, and `$a[8]` is normalised to `$a["8"]` at the subscript rather than converted — so write `string $k`, and convert inside the body if the loop wants another type

error[E0723]: an array's key binding is a `string`, not `string|int`
   --> %s:30:16
